--unwind 6
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Captures are the trailing parameters. They were appended right after the
given arguments, so `m(1)` for `def m(a, b=2)` capturing k bound b = k and
k = 0 (a false proof of a wrong result). Positional defaults were also
aligned with the keyword-only parameters, so `m(1, c=7)` bound b = 0.
